WEBVTT

00:02.235 --> 00:04.936
♪ it seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.938 --> 00:08.407
♪ is violence in movies
and sex on tv ♪

00:08.409 --> 00:11.810
♪ but where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.812 --> 00:14.813
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.815 --> 00:18.417
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.419 --> 00:21.787
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.789 --> 00:23.288
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.290 --> 00:24.589
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.591 --> 00:30.329
♪ he's... A...
Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.969 --> 00:38.937
Welcome, all,
to james woods high's

00:38.939 --> 00:40.205
Annual college fair,

00:40.207 --> 00:42.374
Where each year,
our seniors gather to decide

00:42.376 --> 00:45.277
Where they will go
in the fall to get hpv.

00:46.713 --> 00:49.181
Wow, meg,
so many choices.

00:49.183 --> 00:50.982
Yeah.
There's a state college

00:50.984 --> 00:53.885
With an incredibly offensive
native american mascot.

00:53.887 --> 00:55.721
I'm drunky!

00:55.723 --> 00:58.290
The dakota university mascot!

00:58.292 --> 01:00.058
Look how drunk I am!

01:00.060 --> 01:03.028
This is important for sports!

01:03.030 --> 01:04.229
(gasps)
oh, look,

01:04.231 --> 01:06.131
You can go to
oral roberts.

01:07.500 --> 01:09.868
Peter:
Oh, and there's anal roberts.

01:09.870 --> 01:13.071
Oh, boy, that is a tough,
tough place to get into, lois.

01:13.073 --> 01:14.539
That is tough,
but once you're in there,

01:14.541 --> 01:16.575
You'd be surprised
how much you like it.

01:16.577 --> 01:17.809
Ah, mr. And mrs. Griffin.

01:17.811 --> 01:18.910
So glad
you could make it.

01:18.912 --> 01:20.479
You know, meg has
attracted interest

01:20.481 --> 01:21.847
From several colleges.

01:21.849 --> 01:23.081
Meg going to college.

01:23.083 --> 01:25.217
I always thought she was
gonna be one of those ladies

01:25.219 --> 01:27.686
Who wears a jean jacket
and hangs out at the bar

01:27.688 --> 01:29.221
In a chain restaurant.

01:29.223 --> 01:32.090
Hey. You know you can get
a slice of pineapple

01:32.092 --> 01:34.526
On your burger here.

01:34.528 --> 01:36.061
Hey, jimmy,
another water.

01:36.063 --> 01:37.562
I call miller lite "water."

01:37.564 --> 01:39.531
Jimmy knows me,
he knows that.

01:39.533 --> 01:41.066
Come on, hockey team!

01:41.068 --> 01:43.402
This one's on me.

01:43.404 --> 01:45.270
Merry christmas, meg.

01:45.272 --> 01:47.406
You really think meg
is college material,

01:47.408 --> 01:48.540
Principal shepherd?

01:48.542 --> 01:50.375
Yeah, she's
a solid b student

01:50.377 --> 01:51.777
And that's quite
an accomplishment,

01:51.779 --> 01:54.012
Considering none of her teachers
are willing to sleep with her.

01:54.014 --> 01:55.914
Sophomore year,
she was molested by the janitor.

01:55.916 --> 01:56.782
Does that help?

01:56.784 --> 01:58.183
(laughs)
mr. Griffin,

01:58.185 --> 02:00.719
I believe they're
called "custodians."

02:00.721 --> 02:03.255
Anyway, I was able to get meg
an interview this weekend

02:03.257 --> 02:05.424
At green mountain college
in vermont.

02:05.426 --> 02:06.725
Green mountain college?!

02:06.727 --> 02:09.027
Oh, my god!
That's my first choice!

02:09.029 --> 02:10.896
Can one of you guys
take me up there?

02:10.898 --> 02:13.865
Meg, please excuse your mother
and I for a moment.

02:13.867 --> 02:15.367
We need to work out
our schedules.

02:16.869 --> 02:21.106
(peter and lois
punching, grunting)

02:22.642 --> 02:24.543
I'd be happy
to take you, meg.

02:28.214 --> 02:29.548
Announcer:
We now return to

02:29.550 --> 02:32.651
<i>Extreme makeover:
Bethenny frankel edition.</i>

02:32.653 --> 02:35.520
Crowd:
Move! That! Bus!

02:37.156 --> 02:39.791
Put! That! Bus! Back!

02:39.793 --> 02:41.126
Hey, can you guys
turn that down?

02:41.128 --> 02:41.960
I'm trying to read.

02:41.962 --> 02:43.061
Oh, shut up, brian.

02:43.063 --> 02:44.062
We were here first.

02:44.064 --> 02:46.498
Yeah, brian,
go read in your own room!

02:46.500 --> 02:48.133
I don't have my own room.

02:48.135 --> 02:49.901
Yes, you do.
You have that wicker basket

02:49.903 --> 02:50.802
In the laundry room

02:50.804 --> 02:52.304
With the
frayed bath mat in it.

02:52.306 --> 02:54.840
God, I can't get any
peace and quiet in this house.

02:54.842 --> 02:57.342
Well, now you know how
I felt at mardi gras.

02:57.344 --> 02:59.444
(applause, cheering)

02:59.446 --> 03:01.413
Hey! Keep it down!

03:01.415 --> 03:03.148
I'm trying to get
some sleep up here!

03:03.150 --> 03:05.083
Man:
Show us your boobs...!

03:05.085 --> 03:06.418
My boobs?

03:06.420 --> 03:08.153
Wait, I-I don't think I...

03:09.589 --> 03:11.456
Oh, my! Jewelry!

03:11.458 --> 03:13.992
Ah, I wonder what I'll get
for showing this.

03:13.994 --> 03:17.529
The rules of this city
are very unclear.

03:20.666 --> 03:23.435
(sighs)
this is actually very pleasant.

03:23.437 --> 03:25.804
(crashing)

03:25.806 --> 03:28.306
Hey. Who the hell
knocked over the garbage ca--

03:28.308 --> 03:29.941
Whoa. Whoa. Whoa. Whoa.
Hey. Hey. Hey.

03:29.943 --> 03:30.876
I-I don't want
any trouble.

03:30.878 --> 03:32.210
(laughs):
Well, you in the wrong place

03:32.212 --> 03:33.979
If you ain't looking for
trouble, boy.

03:33.981 --> 03:35.614
<i>Nothin' but trouble
out here.</i>

03:35.616 --> 03:38.884
Big ol' hoot-owl come down,
scoop you up, take your eye out.

03:38.886 --> 03:40.285
All right.
Well, can you at least

03:40.287 --> 03:41.887
Clean this stuff up
when you're done?

03:41.889 --> 03:43.555
It's... Otherwise it's gonna
start to smell.

03:43.557 --> 03:45.891
Oh... You don't like
smell, huh?

03:45.893 --> 03:47.559
Well, sniff on this!

03:47.561 --> 03:48.627
(yells)

03:48.629 --> 03:49.694
(laughs)

03:49.696 --> 03:52.531
Yeah! You got that stink
all up on you, now!

03:52.533 --> 03:53.999
(maniacally barking)

03:54.001 --> 03:55.700
(screams)

03:55.702 --> 03:56.635
Oh, my god!

03:56.637 --> 03:57.869
What is that smell?!

03:57.871 --> 03:59.538
(barking continues)

03:59.540 --> 04:01.640
(yells)
it's like a burning tire dump

04:01.642 --> 04:02.874
Right in my nose!

04:02.876 --> 04:04.209
(yelling)

04:04.211 --> 04:06.378
(hysterically crying):
Brian, why are you doing this?!

04:06.380 --> 04:08.346
We're sorry...!

04:08.348 --> 04:09.247
(stewie yells)

04:09.249 --> 04:11.683
(brian and stewie
yelling, grunting)

04:11.685 --> 04:13.051
Ah! You bastard!

04:13.053 --> 04:14.819
(barking)

04:14.821 --> 04:15.820
(brian grunts)

04:15.822 --> 04:17.656
I can't see!
I'm blind!

04:17.658 --> 04:18.523
(yells)

04:18.525 --> 04:21.226
(grunting)

04:21.228 --> 04:23.428
Ah! What is that smell?

04:23.430 --> 04:24.563
(barking)

04:24.565 --> 04:25.530
Oh, my god!

04:25.532 --> 04:27.699
Brian got sprayed
by a skunk!

04:27.701 --> 04:29.034
No! Not against the wall.

04:29.036 --> 04:31.136
You're gonna scare off
the cockroaches.

04:34.907 --> 04:36.207
Oh, that's not good.

04:36.209 --> 04:40.111
They were 70% of the structure
of this house.

04:40.113 --> 04:43.548
Peter, please tell me this is
covered by our insurance.

04:43.550 --> 04:44.449
Sorry, lois,

04:44.451 --> 04:46.952
It doesn't cover
acts of "dog."

04:50.356 --> 04:52.657
(plays rimshot)

04:58.397 --> 05:00.632
Hey, guys,
I-I think the tomato juice

05:00.634 --> 05:02.634
Is really working. Don't you?

05:02.636 --> 05:06.237
No. You smell like
my six-foot-tall
german girlfriend.

05:06.239 --> 05:09.407
Christopher, are you ready
to go to the guttenschvartzen?

05:09.409 --> 05:10.909
<i>Hell, da!</i>

05:10.911 --> 05:13.979
She can swim across the pool
in two strokes.

05:15.414 --> 05:17.382
Wh... I don't know
what else to do.

05:17.384 --> 05:18.717
I do.

05:18.719 --> 05:22.887
Until the smell wears off,
you're staying outside!

05:22.889 --> 05:25.390
Outside? Lois,
I'm an inside dog!

05:25.392 --> 05:27.926
I'm an inside dog!
I'm sorry, brian,

05:27.928 --> 05:30.562
But you stink.

05:30.564 --> 05:32.597
(chuckles)
I'll take smelling good

05:32.599 --> 05:34.599
Over walking good any day.

05:34.601 --> 05:36.568
Bonnie: You don't
smell good, joe.

05:36.570 --> 05:39.237
I'm sorry,
I thought I was alone.

05:44.677 --> 05:46.811
(shivering)

05:46.813 --> 05:48.146
Morning, brian.

05:48.148 --> 05:50.315
Ew! You still
really stink.

05:50.317 --> 05:52.317
Yeah, you smell like
the meatball sub

05:52.319 --> 05:54.152
I left under
the couch.

05:54.154 --> 05:57.455
<i>Damn it, I just gave away my
hiding place for meatball subs!</i>

05:57.457 --> 06:01.459
<i>I-I'll tell you where
there definitely aren't
any meatball subs--</i>

06:01.461 --> 06:04.029
The side pocket
of my golf bag.

06:04.031 --> 06:05.864
<i>Geez, peter, shut up!</i>

06:05.866 --> 06:07.532
Did you sleep okay
out here, brian?

06:07.534 --> 06:10.101
No! I was so cold.
And you have no idea

06:10.103 --> 06:12.937
How many terrifying things
there are out here in the dark.

06:12.939 --> 06:16.107
My nephew, scrappy brian,
didn't even make it
through the night.

06:16.109 --> 06:17.609
(rustling)

06:17.611 --> 06:20.045
Hey, uncle brian, let's
go check out that noise.

06:20.047 --> 06:21.346
I don't know, scrappy brian.

06:21.348 --> 06:23.214
It might be better
just to stay put.

06:23.216 --> 06:25.216
Aw, I'm not afraid!
Let me at 'em!

06:25.218 --> 06:26.785
Let me at 'em!

06:28.721 --> 06:30.221
(screeches)

06:30.223 --> 06:33.625
Damn it! I told my sister
this wasn't a good weekend.

06:39.999 --> 06:42.467
Hey, bri. How's
it going out there?

06:42.469 --> 06:44.469
Oh, boy, I need this cold air.

06:44.471 --> 06:47.138
They got the heat
cranked up so high in here,

06:47.140 --> 06:49.307
Lois is walking around
without a shirt.

06:49.309 --> 06:50.675
Oh, come on, stewie.

06:50.677 --> 06:52.811
Hey, throw me a jacket
or something, huh?

06:52.813 --> 06:54.045
Nope. You'll stink it up.

06:54.047 --> 06:55.513
Also, since
you've been out there,

06:55.515 --> 06:57.982
I've stopped sneezing,
so this might be permanent.

06:57.984 --> 07:00.218
Well, at least throw me down
some food or something.

07:00.220 --> 07:02.020
Well, I'm afraid
I finished my dinner.

07:02.022 --> 07:04.656
All I have is a steak,
but that belongs to rupert.

07:04.658 --> 07:07.559
Can I have it?
I don't know, that's
a question for rupert.

07:07.561 --> 07:09.661
You'll have to ask him.

07:09.663 --> 07:12.163
Uh... Hey, rupe.

07:12.165 --> 07:13.665
"rupe"? Oh, no. No, no.

07:13.667 --> 07:15.066
No, this is already over.

07:15.068 --> 07:16.901
Come on, stewie, I'm starving.

07:16.903 --> 07:18.670
Good lord, brian,
get a hold of yourself.

07:18.672 --> 07:20.371
You're in a suburban yard.

07:20.373 --> 07:23.341
What kind of dog
can't live outside?

07:23.343 --> 07:24.943
God, he's right.

07:24.945 --> 07:27.212
I'm a disgrace to my species.

07:27.214 --> 07:29.681
Like that gumball machine
traffic cop.

07:30.683 --> 07:33.151
(horns honking, alarms blaring)

07:34.754 --> 07:37.522
Oh, my god, o'connor's
a disaster out there.

07:37.524 --> 07:40.258
It's not his fault.
He was a great
gumball machine--

07:40.260 --> 07:42.627
They just shouldn't
have promoted him.

07:46.065 --> 07:48.032
Oh, I think we're
getting close here.

07:48.034 --> 07:49.400
Meg, what are
you doing?

07:49.402 --> 07:51.136
Just letting the wind
wave my hand.

07:51.138 --> 07:53.138
Sometimes I like
to pretend that I'm flying.

07:53.140 --> 07:55.807
Plus, it tickles.
That's stupid.

07:58.911 --> 08:01.045
(laughing):
Hey-hey-hey...

08:01.047 --> 08:03.114
The wind wants my
hand to go back,

08:03.116 --> 08:04.616
But I'm not letting it.

08:04.618 --> 08:07.485
I'm stronger than it.

08:07.487 --> 08:09.888
Oh, my god, dad,
you lost your hand!

08:09.890 --> 08:12.390
That's all right.
I can regenerate.

08:16.662 --> 08:19.063
(deep, evil voice):
My name is retep,

08:19.065 --> 08:21.232
And I am evil.

08:23.235 --> 08:24.335
(stomach growls)

08:24.337 --> 08:26.604
Come on, brian,
you can find your own food.

08:26.606 --> 08:28.807
Every animal finds its prey.

08:33.746 --> 08:35.747
♪ love in an elevator... ♪

08:35.749 --> 08:37.749
Dude! Check it out!

08:37.751 --> 08:38.917
(tires squeal)

08:38.919 --> 08:40.852
(flies screaming)

08:40.854 --> 08:43.321
All right, I can do this.

08:53.265 --> 08:56.367
Holy crap, I'm so much faster
on all fours!

08:56.369 --> 08:57.936
(grunting)

08:57.938 --> 09:00.104
What's that big rock
doing there?

09:01.106 --> 09:03.641
(sinister laughing)

09:03.643 --> 09:06.778
(bird chirping quietly)

09:06.780 --> 09:09.848
Now, go on, get out of here,
you little bastard.

09:12.218 --> 09:13.551
(crunch)

09:14.353 --> 09:16.187
(crunching)

09:16.189 --> 09:18.323
I did it.
I caught a bird.

09:18.325 --> 09:20.058
I caught a bird! Yes!

09:20.060 --> 09:22.227
Fear me! Aah...!

09:22.229 --> 09:24.295
Aah! I feel so alive!

09:24.297 --> 09:27.699
(exhales)
I feel like a dude who
just touched his first vagina.

09:27.701 --> 09:29.868
Hey. Pound it.

09:29.870 --> 09:31.936
Cool baby.

09:35.407 --> 09:37.075
Well, I called
and confirmed

09:37.077 --> 09:39.077
My interview
for tomorrow morning.

09:39.079 --> 09:41.346
I ordered you nothing.

09:41.348 --> 09:43.014
What else is new?

09:43.016 --> 09:46.017
(intro to "night moves"
by bob seger plays)

09:46.019 --> 09:47.685
Hey, "night moves"!

09:47.687 --> 09:50.154
At least there's one cool
person in this dump.

09:50.156 --> 09:52.223
I wonder who
played this.
I did.

09:52.225 --> 09:53.725
<i>You played
"night moves"?</i>

09:53.727 --> 09:55.927
How would you even know
what that song is?

09:55.929 --> 09:57.729
From you. Dad,
I've been hearing that song

09:57.731 --> 10:00.531
In the backseat of your car
since I was a little kid.

10:00.533 --> 10:02.533
Huh. I never knew
you were listening.

10:02.535 --> 10:04.202
Never even knew
you were there.

10:04.204 --> 10:06.604
Wait, were you that little
fat boy with the glasses?

10:06.606 --> 10:09.741
<i>Yes, dad.
I know a lot about you.</i>

10:09.743 --> 10:12.010
You do?
I know you're afraid
of guacamole.

10:12.012 --> 10:13.344
It's the devil's vomit.

10:13.346 --> 10:15.513
In the last election,
you voted for mighty mouse.

10:15.515 --> 10:18.016
Time to put the might-mouse
in the white house, meg.

10:18.018 --> 10:20.051
<i>And I know you
love augustus gloop.
(giggles)</i>

10:20.053 --> 10:22.720
And you hate mike teavee.
Oh, don't even
say his name.

10:22.722 --> 10:24.856
And you know a lot
about me, right?

10:24.858 --> 10:28.693
♪ out past the cornfields
where the woods got heavy ♪

10:28.695 --> 10:31.562
(motorcycle approaching)
♪ out in the backseat
of my '60 chevy ♪

10:31.564 --> 10:33.965
(motorcycle driving away)
♪ working on mysteries ♪

10:33.967 --> 10:35.800
♪ without any clues... ♪

10:35.802 --> 10:40.271
(sighs) dad, sometimes I wonder
why you even had a family.

10:40.273 --> 10:42.307
I don't know, it's just,
I was dating your mother,

10:42.309 --> 10:44.542
I don't like the
way condoms feel,
next thing you know,

10:44.544 --> 10:47.445
I got a mortgage, a
kid, and a crappy job
at a toy factory.

10:47.447 --> 10:49.547
I thought you liked working
at the toy factory.

10:49.549 --> 10:52.417
Hell no. I always wanted
to be a podiatrist.

10:52.419 --> 10:54.485
Thanks to you, dr. Griffin,
my bunion is healed

10:54.487 --> 10:56.287
And I can walk
without pain.

10:56.289 --> 11:00.258
This isn't a joke. I once had
legitimate aspirations.

11:00.260 --> 11:02.393
You never got
to pursue your dream.

11:02.395 --> 11:04.429
No wonder you hate me.

11:04.431 --> 11:05.763
I don't hate you, meg.

11:05.765 --> 11:07.465
You're my kid.

11:11.236 --> 11:12.270
Who had
the chicken parm?

11:12.272 --> 11:13.571
Oh, that's my
second entree.

11:13.573 --> 11:15.907
But you know what?
You have it, meg.

11:15.909 --> 11:17.408
Thanks, dad.

11:17.410 --> 11:19.978
Boy, after all this food,

11:19.980 --> 11:21.846
We're gonna have
a couple of "night moves"

11:21.848 --> 11:23.781
Back at the motel later,
huh, dad?

11:23.783 --> 11:26.417
Oh, absolutely. You know, that's
what this song's about, meg.

11:26.419 --> 11:27.919
It is?
Oh, yeah.

11:27.921 --> 11:30.588
All of bob seger's songs are
about taking dumps at night.

11:30.590 --> 11:33.024
Uh, "night moves,"
"like a rock,"

11:33.026 --> 11:35.493
"shakedown,"
"the fire down below."

11:35.495 --> 11:38.730
"against the wind" was him
poopin' out of a car.

11:39.698 --> 11:40.698
Quick!

11:40.700 --> 11:42.900
Someone give me
my notebook!

11:46.138 --> 11:47.705
Well, here we are.

11:47.707 --> 11:50.074
Oh, my god, meg,
there's a keg party!

11:52.211 --> 11:55.346
Let's go. If we meet any
chicks, you're my daughter.

11:59.818 --> 12:02.153
Yes!
Yeah! College!

12:02.155 --> 12:04.022
Oh, god, I got
to take a whiz.

12:04.024 --> 12:06.124
Yeah, I got to whiz, too.

12:09.728 --> 12:11.729
(giggles)
sword fight!

12:11.731 --> 12:13.231
Gonna get ya!

12:13.233 --> 12:16.501
You got a funny little wiener,
but you're a nice guy, meg.

12:16.503 --> 12:18.369
This is great, dad.
I know!

12:18.371 --> 12:20.204
I'm having even more fun
than when I...

12:20.206 --> 12:24.542
<i>I mean, than when
we went fiona apple-picking.</i>

12:25.544 --> 12:27.378
Dad, they're all bruised
and filthy.

12:27.380 --> 12:29.213
Yeah, these might be
throwin'-at-buses apples,

12:29.215 --> 12:31.215
Not eatin' apples.
See, meg?

12:31.217 --> 12:34.419
You can be in the flashback
'cause we're friends now.

12:34.421 --> 12:36.487
(wind blowing)

12:49.935 --> 12:51.736
Hey, brian.
(sniffs)

12:51.738 --> 12:53.237
Hey, you don't even smell
like skunk anymore.

12:53.239 --> 12:54.505
Why are you still
out here?

12:54.507 --> 12:56.374
There's nothing
inside for me anymore.

12:56.376 --> 12:57.575
I've moved on.

12:57.577 --> 12:58.776
(hawks, spits)

12:58.778 --> 13:01.746
There was a boo-ger
in that spit, wasn't there?

13:01.748 --> 13:02.747
Stewie, leave me alone.

13:02.749 --> 13:04.215
This is where I belong,

13:04.217 --> 13:05.917
Out here in the wild.

13:05.919 --> 13:06.918
The wild?

13:06.920 --> 13:08.453
You're standing
on the driveway.

13:08.455 --> 13:10.688
Come on.
Hey, hey! Let go of me!

13:10.690 --> 13:12.290
(growling)

13:12.292 --> 13:14.625
I can't believe it.
You've become a wild animal.

13:14.627 --> 13:17.595
You're like that tiger
from siegfried and roy.

13:18.564 --> 13:21.532
Um, I think we all know
the answer to this,

13:21.534 --> 13:23.968
But should I get tested?

13:28.373 --> 13:30.441
(meg and peter laughing)

13:31.910 --> 13:33.244
You guys are back!

13:33.246 --> 13:35.213
Meg, how was
your interview?

13:35.215 --> 13:36.547
Ah, we didn't go.

13:36.549 --> 13:38.149
I slept
right through it.

13:38.151 --> 13:38.916
What?!

13:38.918 --> 13:39.917
Yeah, it was awesome.

13:39.919 --> 13:41.219
We stayed up all night partying.

13:41.221 --> 13:43.054
By the way,
if a girl named rachel calls,

13:43.056 --> 13:45.590
It's a wrong number,
but do tell me that she called.

13:45.592 --> 13:47.258
Where's your
wedding ring?

13:47.260 --> 13:49.327
Yeah, so we missed the
interview, so that's a shame.

13:49.329 --> 13:51.262
Meg, how could you
miss your interview?

13:51.264 --> 13:53.264
That school was
your first choice.

13:53.266 --> 13:55.600
(phone rings inside house)
I'll get it!

13:55.602 --> 13:56.934
It doesn't matter, mom.

13:56.936 --> 13:58.469
Dad and I had
a great time.

13:58.471 --> 13:59.904
We went to a party!

13:59.906 --> 14:02.573
We bonded for the first time
in our lives.

14:02.575 --> 14:04.075
It was just joe.

14:04.077 --> 14:05.610
Meg, how could you blow
your chance

14:05.612 --> 14:07.411
To go
to your first-choice college?

14:07.413 --> 14:10.181
I can't believe
you would be so irresponsible.

14:10.183 --> 14:12.517
Hey, meg, you want to huck
some water balloons at nerds?

14:12.519 --> 14:14.252
Sure!

14:14.254 --> 14:15.653
What the hell?!

14:15.655 --> 14:17.655
(giggles)
(mimics giggle poorly)

14:17.657 --> 14:20.124
We'll work on the laugh,
but you'll get there.

14:20.126 --> 14:21.726
To the meg-copter!

14:25.197 --> 14:26.831
Huh, look down there.

14:26.833 --> 14:28.766
That looks like me
with a green shirt.

14:28.768 --> 14:30.501
He's murdering a lady.

14:30.503 --> 14:32.937
(retep laughs sinisterly)

14:40.779 --> 14:41.879
Dinner's getting cold.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.548
I wonder where your father
and meg are.

14:43.550 --> 14:46.617
They left for the movies
five hours ago.

14:48.287 --> 14:51.289
God, look at lois picking food
from her teeth with her nail.

14:51.291 --> 14:52.890
Someone should tell her
she's a pig.

14:52.892 --> 14:54.058
Mom, you're a pig!

14:54.060 --> 14:55.626
No, you're not supposed
to actually do it!

14:55.628 --> 14:56.961
We were
just talking here!

14:56.963 --> 14:59.030
Oh, now she's crying.
That's not what I wanted.

14:59.032 --> 15:01.032
Stop crying, you bitch!

15:01.034 --> 15:03.167
(groans)
I got to get brian back
in the house.

15:03.169 --> 15:04.902
It's just not the same
without him here.

15:04.904 --> 15:08.206
It's like arnold schwarzenegger
without an accent.

15:08.208 --> 15:09.540
It might be a tumor.

15:09.542 --> 15:11.542
(american accent):
It's not a tumor.

15:15.981 --> 15:18.216
Where are you two
going now?

15:18.218 --> 15:21.385
We're going two places:
None of yo and beeswax.

15:21.387 --> 15:23.221
Clean slam! Come on, meg!

15:23.223 --> 15:26.324
Meg, I'm glad you're having
a good time with your father,

15:26.326 --> 15:28.993
But don't let him distract you
from your priorities.

15:28.995 --> 15:31.862
Remember, you still have
a chance to get into college.

15:31.864 --> 15:33.531
Mom, we're just having fun.

15:33.533 --> 15:35.866
I've never had a good
time with dad before.

15:35.868 --> 15:37.735
I'm just saying,
it's not easy

15:37.737 --> 15:39.737
Dealing with
your father's craziness.

15:39.739 --> 15:41.405
Believe me,
this is no job

15:41.407 --> 15:43.608
<i>For the family's
designated schmendrick.</i>

15:43.610 --> 15:45.876
Trust me, mom.
I know what I'm doing.

15:45.878 --> 15:47.211
That's what
your father said

15:47.213 --> 15:50.047
Before he took that walking tour
of providence.

15:50.049 --> 15:51.882
This is where a homeless
man ate the finger

15:51.884 --> 15:53.251
Of another
homeless man.

15:53.253 --> 15:55.753
This is where some teenagers
beat a gay guy to death.

15:55.755 --> 15:58.723
This building used to be
irish. Now it's cambodian.

15:58.725 --> 16:00.958
And this is where fake
tour guides throw rocks

16:00.960 --> 16:02.627
And steal
tourists' wallets.

16:02.629 --> 16:04.862
Oh, yeah, I read
about this part on yelp.

16:13.639 --> 16:15.706
Peter (quietly):
Meg.

16:17.042 --> 16:19.110
Meg.

16:20.412 --> 16:22.480
Come on.

16:23.415 --> 16:25.483
(ostrich squawking)

16:27.619 --> 16:29.787
Come on, it'll be fun.

16:33.725 --> 16:35.393
(giggles)
isn't this great, meg?

16:35.395 --> 16:36.627
(panting)

16:36.629 --> 16:39.563
Sorry I forgot
to get you an ostrich.

16:43.502 --> 16:44.735
All right, meg, you and me

16:44.737 --> 16:46.337
Are gonna get
something pierced together.

16:46.339 --> 16:47.938
I'll get my ear done.
How about you?

16:47.940 --> 16:50.474
Um, I guess my ears
would be okay.

16:50.476 --> 16:51.942
Oh, come on, meg,
you're my daughter.

16:51.944 --> 16:53.277
Nothing but the best for you.

16:53.279 --> 16:54.345
You're getting the works!

16:54.347 --> 16:55.913
Here, I want everything you got.

16:55.915 --> 16:57.982
Only the best
for my daughter meg.

16:57.984 --> 16:59.250
Ah, look at that.

16:59.252 --> 17:00.918
You look like one of them
beautiful, troubled

17:00.920 --> 17:03.521
Scandinavian youths I've
seen on the porn sites.

17:03.523 --> 17:05.122
You like it?
(muffled):
Mm-hmm.

17:05.124 --> 17:06.757
Awesome. Come on,
let's go next door

17:06.759 --> 17:09.393
And get your mom a funny
refrigerator magnet.

17:13.999 --> 17:16.667
I got a piercing, too.

17:20.839 --> 17:23.307
Hey, lois, guess who made
15 baskets in a row

17:23.309 --> 17:24.842
At the county fair.

17:24.844 --> 17:26.043
Some kid we beat up.

17:26.045 --> 17:27.712
Oh, what a great day!

17:27.714 --> 17:29.347
Had enough yet?
Yes!

17:29.349 --> 17:30.681
I don't know
how you do it.

17:30.683 --> 17:32.616
Everything he does
is exhausting.

17:32.618 --> 17:35.553
Even something as simple
as going to the bank.

17:35.555 --> 17:37.455
Meg, you've probably wondered
from time to time

17:37.457 --> 17:39.523
How on earth I pay
for all my shenanigans.

17:39.525 --> 17:40.858
Well, I'm gonna show you.

17:40.860 --> 17:43.661
This is a robbery! Everybody
get on the (bleep) ground!

17:43.663 --> 17:45.730
If this bitch moves,
shoot him in the eye!

17:45.732 --> 17:47.398
Dad, I don't want
to do this!

17:47.400 --> 17:49.500
You have to! Next week,
we're buying a zebra!

17:49.502 --> 17:51.502
But, dad...
There's no time to argue!

17:51.504 --> 17:52.837
We got 150 seconds

17:52.839 --> 17:54.872
Before the police respond
to the silent alarm!

17:54.874 --> 17:56.540
Now check those
bags for dye packs!

17:56.542 --> 17:58.209
(crying)

17:58.211 --> 17:59.543
Who's the manager here?!

17:59.545 --> 18:00.644
I-I am.

18:00.646 --> 18:02.179
(wailing)

18:02.181 --> 18:03.314
What are you doing?!

18:03.316 --> 18:04.982
You said if he moves,
shoot him!

18:04.984 --> 18:07.184
He's the only one with the
combination to the safe!

18:07.186 --> 18:09.520
It's blown! It's blown!
This whole operation is blown!

18:09.522 --> 18:11.756
I'll get the car.
Kill everyone else.

18:11.758 --> 18:12.990
You've got
to help me, mom.

18:12.992 --> 18:14.191
What do you want me to do?

18:14.193 --> 18:16.360
Please, take him back.

18:16.362 --> 18:17.928
I suppose I could, meg.

18:17.930 --> 18:20.231
But a part of growing up
is learning how to handle

18:20.233 --> 18:23.167
A tough situation on your own,
like getting into college

18:23.169 --> 18:25.236
Or breaking up
with your father.

18:27.172 --> 18:30.274
I guess,
but it's not gonna be easy.

18:30.276 --> 18:32.076
Well, life's not
always easy, meg.

18:32.078 --> 18:34.445
Just ask an
ugly boy scout.

18:34.447 --> 18:37.715
Scoutmaster davenport, you want
to share a tent with me tonight?

18:37.717 --> 18:41.619
Oh, billy, I like
you as a friend.

18:46.892 --> 18:48.726
Brian, you got
to get in here, man.

18:48.728 --> 18:50.961
I've been taking a break
from lois's breast milk,

18:50.963 --> 18:53.097
And her boobs
are enormous.

18:53.099 --> 18:55.299
They're like jiffy pop
just before the foil breaks.

18:55.301 --> 18:57.768
You should come check 'em out
before they get infected.

18:57.770 --> 19:00.237
Yeah, nice try, stewie,
but I'm still not coming inside.

19:00.239 --> 19:02.473
But, brian,
I need you inside.

19:02.475 --> 19:04.575
I'm going crazy in here
without you.

19:04.577 --> 19:06.744
Please, I need
my friend back.

19:06.746 --> 19:08.913
Look, stewie,
I've learned something out here.

19:08.915 --> 19:11.215
You see, living in the wild,
I-I've realized

19:11.217 --> 19:13.250
That all the pain
I've ever had in my life

19:13.252 --> 19:16.454
Has-has come from me always
trying to be something I'm not.

19:16.456 --> 19:19.256
I mean, I'm not a writer,
I'm not an artist,

19:19.258 --> 19:21.125
I'm not an intellectual.

19:21.127 --> 19:23.561
What I am... Is a dog.

19:23.563 --> 19:27.398
And as a dog,
my place is outside.

19:27.400 --> 19:28.732
I'm sorry, stewie,

19:28.734 --> 19:31.735
But nothing will ever
make me come back inside.

19:31.737 --> 19:33.804
(thunder crashing)

19:35.774 --> 19:38.976
Stewie, get the
hell in here!

19:38.978 --> 19:40.277
(chuckles)

19:40.279 --> 19:43.714
That dog sure changed
his mind quick.

19:48.253 --> 19:49.753
Oh, meg, there you are!

19:49.755 --> 19:50.921
Hey, let's put on
fake eyelashes

19:50.923 --> 19:52.423
And flirt with
people on the bus.

19:52.425 --> 19:55.259
Dad, I'm sorry,
but I can't go with you.

19:55.261 --> 19:57.928
Mmm, are you sure?

19:57.930 --> 19:59.463
I called green mountain college.

19:59.465 --> 20:00.998
They let me reschedule
my interview,

20:01.000 --> 20:02.867
So I'm gonna drive
back up there.

20:02.869 --> 20:05.035
It's time for me
to get serious about my life

20:05.037 --> 20:06.770
And take some responsibility.

20:06.772 --> 20:08.639
I don't like this meg.

20:08.641 --> 20:10.107
I like the fun meg!

20:10.109 --> 20:11.842
I thought we were friends.

20:11.844 --> 20:14.044
Dad, I don't need you
to be my friend.

20:14.046 --> 20:16.380
I need you to be my father.

20:16.382 --> 20:18.215
Well, that is too much
to ask, meg.

20:18.217 --> 20:20.217
It's hard being a father.

20:20.219 --> 20:23.020
This is why that woman in texas
drowned all her kids.

20:23.022 --> 20:25.055
I hate the passage of time!

20:25.057 --> 20:27.558
(sobbing):
My little girl's growing up!

20:27.560 --> 20:29.793
(crying)

20:29.795 --> 20:31.795
Yes, she is, dad.

20:31.797 --> 20:33.330
Yes, she is.

20:33.332 --> 20:35.399
("night moves" begins)

20:42.240 --> 20:44.308
<i>Meg:
I did get
into green mountain college,</i>

20:44.310 --> 20:46.677
<i>And contracted hpv
my first night there.</i>

20:46.679 --> 20:48.345
<i>I got nicknamed the warthog,</i>

20:48.347 --> 20:51.415
<i>And, like the hpv,
it stuck for life.</i>

20:55.420 --> 20:57.087
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru